  "title": "Erdős Problem #111",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "If $G$ is a graph let $h_G(n)$ be defined such that any subgraph of $G$ on $n$ vertices can be made bipartite after deleting at most $h_G(n)$ edges.\nWhat is the behaviour of $h_G(n)$? Is it true that $h_G(n)/n\\to \\infty$ for every graph $G$ with chromatic number $\\aleph_1$?",
